user_examples:
Non-streaming example:

import { zodize } from '@redwood/tsdk';
const UserV1 = zodize({ id: 'string', name: 'string', role: 'string' }, { tag: 'role' });
// Runtime: UserV1.zodSchema.parse(obj)
// Type: UserV1.Type

Streaming example (simplified):

import { streamingValidator, zodize } from '@redwood/tsdk';
const Result = zodize({ tag: ['choice','summary'], score: 'number', payload: { text: 'string' } });
const validator = streamingValidator(Result.zodSchema, { mergeStrategy: 'first-wins' });
// For each chunk we call validator.consume(chunk) -> { valid, partial, errors }
// On final chunk: validator.finalize() -> strict parse or throw.
